      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1917, Boice Hardwood Company built a band mill in Hartford, turning the town into a company town centered on lumber.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hartford%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hartford sits at the northeastern tip of the Great Smoky Mountains, surrounded by Snowbird Mountain to the east and Mount Cammerer to the south.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hartford%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Pigeon River Valley, where Hartford lies, divides the Great Smokies crest from the Snowbird massif, shaping the town’s landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hartford%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Hartford’s Pigeon Valley Church, founded in 1889, still bears the town’s original name and reflects its early community life.",
